odo-take/1
name: Ode to Joy
by: Ludwig van Beethoven (1824), the tune alone; written for odo by Claude
about: The first tune to learn: five notes, one finger at a time, all in C major. Then
about: a held note to swell into, and a last note with a slow vibrato.
tempo: 100
meter: 4/4
key: C major
controller: patrickreynolds/grid

score
key C4 major
press 0.6

section First line
say One finger, one square at a time: lift between the notes
bar 1
E4:1 E4:1 F4:1 G4:1
bar 2
G4:1 F4:1 E4:1 D4:1
bar 3
C4:1 C4:1 D4:1 E4:1
bar 4
E4:3/2 D4:1/2 D4:2(swell 0.5 0.8)

section Second line
say The same again, ending on the home note
